WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.380
Four economies face double digit GDP drops as war is set to shrink the region. This is Omni View Africa &amp; Middle East, Episode 21. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Al Jazeera reports the International Monetary Fund expects the Middle East and Central Asia economy to contract in 2026 amid the U.S. Israel War on Iran. Iraq, Bahrain, Kuwait and Qatar are the four economies in that fallout. The fund has cut its goal forecast sharply because the Strait of Hormuz has stayed shut.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.760
It puts the UAE on course for a 3.9% contraction this year.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.140
In the October World Economic Outlook, the fund set an energy supply shock from that conflict

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.120
drove oil prices up 32% this year, close to a third higher.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:49.020
The same shock lifted global inflation to 4.7% and undid two years of cooling prices.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.540
The fund puts global growth at 3% in 2026.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.980
